WEBVTT

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.320
Priss, Linna, Nene!

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:15.320
Why is Galatea targeting us here now?

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.840
You can think about it later.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.290
This might be the last time we change here.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:30.520
A lot of things have happened
to us, haven't they?

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:32.460
Yes, they have.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:39.640
How rude of them!

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.010
Shoo, shoo!

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.840
They're just boomers, so don't worry about them.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:46.320
But...

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.790
Hurry up! They'll break the water
tank and be in here soon.

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:53.850
Hurry up, both of you.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:02.300
Nigel, please proceed.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.290
Okay.

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.470
I have to go through that again,
but I can't stand it!

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.390
It makes your wound sting, doesn't
it? But please be patient.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:26.320
If negative messages are mixed in,
the inner-metal won't fit.

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:28.550
I understand.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:02:59.560
Damn!

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.360
An earthquake again?

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.060
What the hell is going on?!

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.470
What's the situation?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:23.310
It won't hold any longer.

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.110
Who can't swim?

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.580
Me...

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.210
They're coming!

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:00.880
Damn!

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:06.820
Damn!

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:46.620
Sylia!

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.060
Let's go!

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.110
Go ahead!

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.150
Mackey, you too!

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:37.140
Nene!

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:47.990
Let's go!

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:49.150
Come on!

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:53.930
Are you all right?

00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:56.900
Oh, my, that was tough for an old man like me.

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:00.840
Let's go.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:10.570
What the hell?!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:32.300
Is everybody all right?

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.000
Yeah, we're fine.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:40.240
What is this?

00:06:40.780 --> 00:06:43.210
Yuck, it's disgusting!

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:52.390
It's not just here!

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.050
Look!

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.790
Is this Tokyo?

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:40.330
It looks as if it has a completely
different ecosystem.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:43.830
I guess we don't have anywhere to go.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:52.310
Oh, no. Galatea might not
have targeted this place.

00:07:57.550 --> 00:07:58.520
Again?!

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:01.720
Everybody, hurry and get
as far away as possible!

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:17.400
What is that?

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:19.640
Just as I thought.

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:28.220
Coincidentally, this place

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:31.950
seems to be exactly on the Dragon Line
which is spreading the phenomenon.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:58.840
What beautiful scenery!

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:04.680
This is what I've always longed to see.

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.700
No matter where we go, it's the same.

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:14.470
What'll we do?

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:17.050
That place might be okay.

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:46.140
Here I go!

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:53.320
Finally...

00:11:56.430 --> 00:11:58.520
I guess we barely came through.

00:12:00.930 --> 00:12:05.420
For now, I can't think of another place where
boomers wouldn't have an effect.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.800
Surely, there are no boomers here.

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:14.440
But isn't it strange to see a place
without any cleaning boomers?

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:18.510
I guess they all went in search
of their associates,

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:20.410
in order to fuse with each other.

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:24.480
If that's true, we should be safe for a while.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:27.950
Well, it's about time.

00:12:32.700 --> 00:12:33.660
Who's there?!

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:48.580
Don't scare us like that!

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:52.450
I'm surprised to find people still
living in a place like this.

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:03.260
Boomer!

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.700
Oh, don't worry, these are...

00:13:08.200 --> 00:13:09.290
Boomer!

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:14.270
It's a boomer!

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:51.640
Then, when I realized everything
had changed like that,

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:54.580
violent boomers and buildings
that changed shapes.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:57.310
No matter where I ran to,

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:03.920
roads were closed, and we didn't
have any place to go.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:06.390
So we looked for a place where
there weren't any boomers.

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:14.020
Finally, we arrived at this park.

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:18.630
On our way here, there were many victims.

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:22.500
Tada!

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:30.710
What?

00:14:31.950 --> 00:14:33.350
Dummy!

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:47.120
I see. People who didn't have any
way to evacuate gathered here.

00:14:47.730 --> 00:14:51.000
Yes, probably fifty or so.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.470
That many?

00:14:52.470 --> 00:14:53.460
Yes.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:58.860
Still, many people died on their way here.

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:02.930
Here you are.

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:05.540
Thank you.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:09.690
Don't look like that!

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:14.780
We need to thank God that
we've survived such a trial.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:18.630
Yes, you're right, because of my efforts!

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:22.060
You were crying while we
were running, weren't you?

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.460
Don't say things like that!

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:33.310
I'm sorry that I thought you were a boomer.

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:36.470
Oh, no. Sorry to have scared you.

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:43.310
Well, in this situation, anybody would be
scared if someone appeared like that.

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:50.130
Excuse me, but this coffee and
food, how did you get them?

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:52.890
We take turns and go hunting.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:54.160
Hunting?

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:54.430
Yes, that's what we call it.
Hunting?

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.690
Yes, that's what we call it.

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:09.550
How dare they call this hunting!

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:13.640
They made me do this, even
though I'm a police officer!

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.350
The line of boomerization
is right over there,

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:17.950
so we don't have time to complain!

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:19.750
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:29.520
It's here! Get the hell out of there!

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:31.730
Hurry up!

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:41.640
Run!

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:01.200
This is good!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:07.340
See? This is a limited product
sold only in this area!

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:08.940
Just like that!

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:12.840
That story is mine, you idiot!

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:17.470
Here you go.

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:21.240
How about you? You like drinking, don't you?

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:23.980
Yes, I've been drinking already.

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:35.490
Lady, we have lots to drink, so you
can keep going and going! Right?

00:17:41.340 --> 00:17:45.170
By the way, what are your plans now?

00:17:53.080 --> 00:17:56.450
I have to settle this matter once and for all.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:00.820
But how about you?

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:04.020
That's right. Tokyo totally changed last night.

00:18:04.590 --> 00:18:06.820
It's not possible to go hunting anymore.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.220
I guess...

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:10.830
Then that manager harassed me sexually, can
you believe it?! Sexual harassment!

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:12.920
What a jerk!

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:15.160
Isn't he?!

00:19:16.030 --> 00:19:17.470
Hey, are you listening to me?!

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:19.160
I am! I am listening to you!

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.010
What a strange face!

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:26.130
Who let her drink like that?!

00:19:52.270 --> 00:19:55.170
You're so good at doing this.

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.700
You're here, just as I thought.

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:30.740
What are you doing?

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.810
What are these things?

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.210
Mackey!

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:53.920
Mackey!

00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:57.280
Next Episode

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.920
Mackey, who loves to deal with machines.

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:06.190
Mackey, who is as pure and fragile as glass.

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:10.090
I'm not interested in boys who
are younger than I am,

00:21:11.030 --> 00:21:14.160
but... but Mackey...

00:21:15.070 --> 00:21:17.300
I will help you.

00:21:18.310 --> 00:21:20.400
Next Bubblegum Crisis!
